
-----------------------------------------------------
CountDownLatch
---------------------------------------------------

A CountDownLatch is a synchronization tool in Java used when one or more
 threads need to wait until some other tasks finish.
 It works with a counter.
 When counter becomes 0, waiting thread continues.
 ------------------------------------------------------------
Imagine you are waiting for 3 friends before leaving.

Friends arrive one by one:

Friend 1 arrives → count becomes 2
Friend 2 arrives → count becomes 1
Friend 3 arrives → count becomes 0

Now you can leave.

That waiting system = CountDownLatch
------------------------------------------------------------------
Main Use
Use when:
One thread must wait until N tasks complete.
Examples:
Wait for 3 API calls
Wait for 5 files to upload
Wait for 10 worker threads to finish
Wait for startup services ready
-----------------------------------------------------------------------
Constructor
CountDownLatch latch = new CountDownLatch(3);
Means:
Counter starts at 3
Need 3 completions.
--------------------------------------------------------------------
Main Methods (Use of Each)
1. await()
latch.await();
Meaning:
Wait here until count becomes 0.
Used by main/waiting thread.

2. countDown()
latch.countDown();
Meaning:
One task finished. Reduce count by 1.
Used by worker threads.

3. getCount()
latch.getCount();
Returns current remaining count.

4. await(time, unit)
latch.await(5, TimeUnit.SECONDS);
Wait only max 5 seconds.
------------------------------------------------
Real Backend Example
Dashboard API needs:
user data
order data
payment data
Run all in parallel.
Main response waits until all 3 complete.
Use:
CountDownLatch(3)
----------------------------------------------
Important Rule
Latch is one-time use.
Once count reaches 0:
❌ cannot reset

------------------------------------------------
CountDownLatch allows threads to wait until a specified number of operations complete.
